Bundled specialization/spell labels, spell and talent tooltips, talent-tree
relationships, and encounter-journal text are retrieved from Blizzard's Game Data
API. The catalog records its exact namespace, retrieval time, source URLs, and
unavailable records. It contains no icons or private logs.
The software's MIT license does not relicense third-party game content.

Warcraft Logs supplies report data through its official API under each user's
own authorization. Do not distribute credentials or private report caches.

Historical work used Lorrgs (https://github.com/gitarrg/lorrgs, MIT per its README)
to seed spell IDs. This release regenerates labels from Blizzard; it does not
bundle Lorrgs source, its cooldown rules, or SimulationCraft APLs.

Packaged dependencies retain their own licenses in the executable bundle.
